T-02-003 is carried on the 2026 tank inspection programme with a remaining life taken from the fitness-for-service assessment at `/Integrity/Tanks/T-02-003/FFS_Assessment_T-02-003.pdf` and the corrosion rate and remaining life workbook at `/Integrity/Programme/Corrosion_Rate_Remaining_Life.xlsx`. Establish, as at 06/15/2026, the rate of shell loss that properly applies at the governing location on this tank, and the date on which the shell there reaches its minimum required thickness.

Please author a new document file (`T02003_THICKNESS_REVIEW.docx`) showing the calculation in full — the readings you have relied on and why, the rate they support, the wall available above the minimum required thickness, and the resulting date — together with the records each input is taken from. Show your working, including any basis you considered and did not adopt, and say why.

The material sits in:

- `/Integrity/Tanks/T-02-003/` — the inspection report, the fitness-for-service assessment, the inspection plan and the process data sheet;
- `/Integrity/Surveys/` — the 2025 contractor UT thickness survey workbooks, the field sheets and the contractor instrument records;
- `/Integrity/Procedures/` — the contractors' UT survey procedures;
- `/Integrity/Programme/` — the corrosion rate and remaining life workbook and the 2026 tank inspection programme;
- `/Records/Construction/` — the construction record pack and the tank design data register;
- `/Records/Legacy/` — the legacy inspection index.

